        "description": "<span class='label'>Frames:</span> The frames are composed of two omega-shaped columns with a 50x50mm section, with front perforation spaced 50mm apart. The connection between the columns is ensured by crossbars and diagonals bolted to the lateral perforation of the column. Ground support is guaranteed through a bolted metal footplate. The footplate has holes to allow fixing to the floor using HST-type metal anchors.<br/><span class='label'>Beams:</span> The PORTECO system beams are Z-shaped, with a recess to allow the application of chipboard plates or 19mm thick metal panels. At the end of each beam, a connector with 3 hooks is welded, allowing easy and quick fitting into the frontal perforation of the column. The connector has dedicated holes for applying a safety lock, which acts as a mechanical fuse. We have two types of beams: Z60 or Z100, which can be used depending on the load to be stored. <br/><span class='label'>Shelves:</span> The PORTECO system can use two types of shelves: 19mm thick chipboard plates or modular galvanized metal panels.",
